  "steps": [
    "Heat a large stockpot over medium-high heat. Crumble in the ground chuck and sausage and cook, breaking it up, until evenly browned with no pink remaining, 10-12 minutes. Drain off the excess grease.",
    "Add the drained chili beans, spicy chili beans, diced tomatoes with their juice, and tomato paste. Add the onion, celery, green and red bell peppers, chile peppers, bacon bits, bouillon cubes, and beer.",
    "Season with the chili powder, Worcestershire, garlic, oregano, cumin, hot sauce, basil, salt, pepper, cayenne, paprika, and sugar. Stir to blend.",
    "Cover and simmer over low heat for at least 2 hours, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are soft and the chili has thickened. Taste and adjust the salt, pepper, and chili powder.",
    "Ladle over corn chips in bowls and top with shredded Cheddar."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The chili tastes better the longer it simmers, and it reheats well the next day."
  ],
